# Frame, compression on, packet at/above threshold -- full frame per 01 §2 + §3.1 (zlib payload).
# Docs: 01 §2, §3.1, §3.2 (n >= threshold -> VarInt n then zlib stream, default level = 6, header + Adler-32), §3.4;
#       09 §2 threshold 256. Inner packet: 05b 0x7C System Chat, 09 §1 / §3.2 row "System Chat (player chat)".
# Stated inputs: threshold 256; zlib level 6 (python zlib.compress(body, 6), as cc_deflate).
#   Inner packet (play, clientbound, id 0x7c System Chat), 261 bytes uncompressed:
#     content = literal text (network NBT bare String tag, 09 §1) "<Alice> " + message, 256 characters,
#       message = the first 248 characters of 6 x "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. ";
#     overlay = false.
#   Uncompressed packet bytes:
#     7c                       packet id: VarInt 0x7c (System Chat)
#     08                       content: network NBT root tag type 8 (String), no root name
#     01 00                    content String length: UShort 256
#     <256 bytes>              content String data: "<Alice> The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. The quick brown fox jum"
#     00                       overlay: Boolean false

44                                               # frame length: VarInt 68 (Data length VarInt + zlib stream)
85 02                                            # data length: VarInt 261 (uncompressed packet size)
78 9c                                            # zlib header (CMF 0x78, FLG 0x9c: deflate, 32K window, default level)
# deflate data (60 bytes)
ab e1 60 64 b0 71 cc c9 4c 4e b5 53 08 c9 48 55
28 2c cd 4c ce 56 48 2a ca 2f cf 53 48 cb af 50
c8 2a cd 2d 28 56 c8 2f 4b 2d 52 28 01 4a e7 24
